KiTTY is a free (MIT-licensed) Windows Telnet and SSH client. This
manual documents KiTTY, and its companion utilities kscp, ksftp,
klink, kageant and kittygen.

\e{Note to Unix users:} this manual currently primarily documents the
Windows versions of the KiTTY utilities. Some options are therefore
mentioned that are absent from the \i{Unix version}; the Unix version has
features not described here; and the \i\cw{pterm} and command-line
\cw{kittygen} and \cw{kageant} utilities are not described at all. The
only Unix-specific documentation that currently exists is the
\I{man pages for KiTTY tools}man pages.

